Repository: /luxon (Luxon JS date library). Task: apply a small, well-identified fix to /luxon/src/impl/util.js, then verify it.

BUG: `padStart` in /luxon/src/impl/util.js drops the minus sign for negative inputs, so `DateTime#toISODate()` renders negative (BCE) years wrongly (year -1 -> '00-1-01-01' instead of '-0001-01-01').

CURRENT CODE (around lines 101-107):
```js
  export function padStart(input, n = 2) {
    if (input.toString().length < n) {
      return ("0".repeat(n) + input).slice(-n);
    } else {
      return input.toString();
    }
  }
```

REQUIRED FIX (exact):
```js
  export function padStart(input, n = 2) {
    const isNeg = input < 0;
    let padded;
    if (isNeg) {
      padded = "-" + ("" + -input).padStart(n, "0");
    } else {
      padded = ("" + input).padStart(n, "0");
    }
    return padded;
  }
```

IMPORTANT CONCURRENCY: another agent may be concurrently editing /luxon/src/impl/util.js (a change inside `objToLocalTS` about `d.setUTCFullYear(obj.year, obj.month - 1, obj.day)`). Do NOT revert or alter that change if present. Before editing, run `cd /luxon && git diff src/impl/util.js` to see the current state, re-read the file, and make ONLY the padStart change (use a targeted edit of just that function). Never rewrite the whole file. If the padStart fix is already applied, do nothing and report that.

VERIFY (report exact output):
1. `cd /luxon && git diff src/impl/util.js` (report the full diff).
2. `cd /luxon && npx jest test/datetime 2>&1 | tail -20` — the ONLY acceptable failures are the 2 known pre-existing French-locale ones in test/datetime/toFormat.test.js ('FFF'/'FFFF').
3. Ad-hoc check in /tmp (not in the repo test dir) via `cd /luxon && npx babel-node /tmp/padcheck.js` (import from '/luxon/src/luxon.js'): assert `DateTime.fromObject({year:-1, month:1, day:1}).toISODate() === '-0001-01-01'`, year -12 -> '-0012-01-01', year -100 -> '-0100-01-01', year -1234 -> '-1234-01-01', year 5 -> '0005-01-01', year 2020 -> '2020-01-01'. Report exact outputs.
4. `cd /luxon && npx eslint --quiet src/impl/util.js`.

Report concisely: the diff, the test results, the ad-hoc outputs, and any problem.
